> I understand there is general disdain for NethackW with the nice icons
> here.  Can you explain why you feel your disdain is justified?

Personally, I don't disdain tiles per se, but I find that nethack gains a lot
from immersion. To me, immersion comes easiest from either very detailed
graphics that give the right visual sensation by themselves, or graphics so
abstract that my imagination does most of the visual heavy lifting. I find that
the available graphical clients are too far away from the former, while the
text-based clients fit squarely in the latter.


